  "script": {
    "word_count": 225,
    "est_duration_s": 90.0,
    "segments": [
      {
        "id": "seg-01",
        "chapter_id": "ch-01",
        "text": "This is Lake Mead, Nevada, seen from space by Landsat satellites, one summer at a time from 1984 to 2026.",
        "year_from": 1984,
        "year_to": 1984,
        "claim_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-02",
        "chapter_id": "ch-02",
        "text": "Between 1984 and 1991, about 6 percent of the area turned from water to land, mostly in the east. In all, about 220 hectares changed. One report says: Storage in Lake Mead decreased by 323,000 acre-feet in the month prior to February 29, 1984, when it contained 24,045,000 acre-feet.",
        "year_from": 1985,
        "year_to": 1991,
        "claim_ids": [
          "cl-01"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-03",
        "chapter_id": "ch-03",
        "text": "Between 1992 and 1998, about 6 percent of the area turned from land to water, mostly in the east. In all, about 180 hectares changed. One report says: The return of normal rainfall and runoff on the Colorado caused water impounded at Lake Mead to rise back to normal levels, inundating willow root crowns in the delta.",
        "year_from": 1992,
        "year_to": 1998,
        "claim_ids": [
          "cl-03"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-04",
        "chapter_id": "ch-04",
        "text": "Between 1999 and 2010, about a fifth of the area turned from water to land, mostly in the east. Records show: Since 1999, a multi-year drought and increased water demand have caused Lake Mead's water levels to decline.",
        "year_from": 1999,
        "year_to": 2012,
        "claim_ids": [
          "cl-04"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-05",
        "chapter_id": "ch-05",
        "text": "Between 2013 and 2014, about 4 percent of the area turned from water to land, mostly in the east. Part of it may come from switching Landsat satellites. One report says: Excessively arid winters in 2012 and 2013 caused Lake Mead's water level to drop approximately 51 feet since December 2012.",
        "year_from": 2013,
        "year_to": 2014,
        "claim_ids": [
          "cl-05"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg-06",
        "chapter_id": "ch-06",
        "text": "That is how Lake Mead, Nevada has changed since 1984.",
        "year_from": 2015,
        "year_to": 2026,
        "claim_ids": []
      }
